      "title": "RCFC 6(a)(6)(A)'s legal holidays: the § 6103(a) days in force when the\nRCFC time-computation rules here are (2002 onward), plus Inauguration\nDay, which FRCP 6(a)(6) does not name. § 6103(c) makes January 20 \"of\neach fourth year after 1965\" a holiday, as codified by Pub. L. 89-554\n(September 6, 1966; the uncodified Pub. L. 85-1 of 1957 preceded it). It\nstates only the Sunday shift; observing a Saturday Inauguration Day on\nthe Friday before, as § 6103(b)(1) does for every other holiday, is the\ninterpretive choice `packs/clock/SOURCES-NOTES.md` records. The cite is\ntoday's RCFC 6, whose Rules Committee Notes record its changes since\n2002 (Juneteenth added in 2022): a later text, cited for the whole\nhistory on purpose."
